id: pm-context-ci6v
title: "pm context-usage: report which served context an agent actually used"
description: ""
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-25T23:11:58.626Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-10T12:17:18.058Z"
assignee: codex-sol
claim_principal: codex-sol
author: pi-agent
comments[15]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-07T21:10:20.678Z",codex-sol,"Acceptance scenario against the built package and a real scratch tracker before source changes: serve two focus facts in session-a; cite the first, then measure one used of two served facts (precision 0.5), positive unused estimated token cost, and no attribution to session-b. Baseline selects both items but has no context_receipt and no bundle/session metrics. Implement stable section/fact ids for the actually rendered subset, isolated bounded runtime receipts, explicit citation/item/file usage reports, session-aware later SDK touches, and README agent protocol. Existing notes describe the shipped legacy read-only report; the requested receipt measurement extends it without a competing relevance service or host-ledger schema."
  "2026-10-07T21:18:47.276Z",codex-sol,"Implemented the v1 receipt protocol on both serving paths. Facts are derived after rendering so omitted sections and truncated body text stay outside the denominator. Explicit receipt-scoped citations, successful item-mutation reports and file-edit reports are idempotent and session isolated; estimates disclose four-character token approximation and proxy limitations. Storage uses bounded atomic runtime snapshots separate from the SDK ledger. Built-package acceptance passes for two focus facts, one citation, precision 0.5 and an untouched independent session. The SDK touch ledger lacks session/fact ids and a generic fact-level post-egress callback, so hooks report usage explicitly and complete file delivery is documented."
  "2026-10-07T21:24:29.410Z",codex-sol,"Behavioral revert proof: with tests unchanged, rebuilding after restoring raw-output-only measureContextOutput makes the built acceptance test execute and fail at the missing-receipt assertion. Rebuilding after disabling only recordReceiptUsage persistence makes the same test execute and fail at used_facts actual 0 expected 1. Restoring both functions passes that identical test. Initial npm run release:check passes the exact unchanged 100% line/branch/function thresholds across six configured source files; nine receipt tests and 295 total tests pass."
  "2026-10-07T21:26:26.047Z",codex-sol,"Both npm run release:check and bun run release:check pass: 295 tests, zero failures, unchanged 100% line/branch/function gates across six configured sources; docstrings, production audit, packaging and release workflow checks pass. Fresh packed npm and Bun consumers activated the package with the real CLI under Node and native Bun: two served focus facts, one explicit citation, precision 0.5, positive unused token estimate, and a JSON handoff receipt. Documentation records the behavioral revert assertions, runtime retention and SDK session/post-egress limitations. The owner item has no dependency edges."
  "2026-10-07T21:27:02.675Z",codex-sol,"The first pm test --run --progress attempt exposed linked-run environment isolation: its schema context supplies a tracker path which SDK init can select ahead of a cwd-only fixture. The fixture now supplies both explicit cwd and pmRoot, so every initialized tracker stays disposable even under linked-test execution. The failed linked run made no item test-result writes because this tracker has test-result tracking disabled; results are documented in comments instead. Rerunning the linked commands verifies the corrected boundary."
  "2026-10-07T21:28:08.049Z",codex-sol,"Final linked-test verification passes: pm test pm-context-ci6v --run --progress executes both registered commands successfully (nine receipt tests plus the one built-package acceptance test). Real file edits and SDK item updates precede their proxy submissions. Fixtures explicitly pin cwd and pmRoot and remain isolated under the linked schema context. Repeating both behavioral reverts with the final test file again fails on missing receipt and used_facts 0 versus 1, then passes after restoration. The claim is released for review; the item remains open for orchestrator verification. All implementation, documentation, linked tests and history evidence will ship together in the change commit."
  "2026-10-07T21:31:49.139Z",codex-sol,"Exact-commit verification exposed a nondeterministic branch in the rotation fixture: equal filesystem timestamps happened only on some runs. The fixture now explicitly sets equal timestamp pairs, preserving the deterministic filename tie-break test and exact coverage threshold. Final review also tightened editable-file matching to complete rendered text links or exact JSON string values, with regressions for partial filename mentions and JSON-escaped quoted filenames. No new test count or gate exemption is introduced."
  "2026-10-07T21:32:43.438Z",codex-sol,"The final linked receipt suite and built acceptance command both pass after the deterministic rotation and exact file-link regressions. Both independent behavioral reverts still execute and fail at their expected receipt/used-fact assertions, and restoration passes. Releasing the claim for review; the amended implementation/evidence commit will be checked again under both release commands and as packed Node/native Bun consumers."
  "2026-10-10T02:50:04.198Z",codex,"Orchestrator verified review 4213980426 against real filesystem receipts: under clock skew the old retention logic deletes the newly returned receipt (retained count 0 versus required 1). The existing retention test now fails before the repair and passes when the current receipt is excluded before sorting the other snapshots. The hard retained-count bound remains intact. Full release gate running. Companion owner pm-cli-website-session-2026-10-10."
  "2026-10-10T02:57:26.501Z",codex,"Orchestrator full release:check passed after the receipt-retention repair. The configured gate measures lines, branches and functions at 100%; it does not independently measure statements, so this is not four-metric certification. The new real-filesystem regression failed on unchanged logic (retained receipt count 0) and passed on the repair. Existing count, oversize, atomic-write and failure cleanup assertions remain. Preparing the exact review head."
  "2026-10-10T12:03:16.587Z",codex-sol,"Renew PR 131 from clean head aaa5743 against main 49f1594. Preserve receipt and context-usage behavior and the real future-mtime retention regression. Merge normally, regenerate artifacts with tsc, adopt published SDK 2026.10.10 with its actual installed contracts, retain independent compatibility floor 2026.8.15, and renew full release, linked, retention and packed-consumer evidence. Historical SDK 2026.10.4 receipts do not certify this merged candidate. No merge, publish or review requests by this agent."
  "2026-10-10T12:08:49.866Z",codex-sol,"Main merged normally; only dist/index.js.map conflicted and tsc regenerated it from the auto-merged release metadata and receipt source. Exact development SDK 2026.10.10 installed with pm-ops 2026.10.6 and pm-changelog 2026.10.5; package/manifest/runtime remain 2026.10.10 and peer/manifest floors remain 2026.8.15. Full release check passes 295 tests, zero failures or skips. Both existing linked commands pass within their unchanged 240-second deadlines. Independently repeated the original source-only future-mtime control: real retention assertion fails at 0 versus 1, then restoring byte-identical source passes. Configured LCOV covers six of eleven authored executable files: 3278/3278 lines, 1038/1038 branches, 219/219 functions; no independent statement counter. Docstring gate checks nine TypeScript files and 31 rule-selected declarations. Broader c8 measurement of ten JavaScript/TypeScript files reports 3809/3857 statements and lines, 1154/1160 branches, 103/104 functions; shell coverage remains unmeasured. This does not establish whole-source four-metric certification. Both production and development audits report zero vulnerabilities."
  "2026-10-10T12:12:33.570Z",codex-sol,"Source renewal committed as c0de977 with normal merge parents aaa5743 and 49f1594. Fresh npm/Node and Bun/native Bun packed consumers pass under SDK 2026.10.10 and minimum 2026.8.15: governed built harness, installed CLI, two served/one used facts, precision 0.5, session isolation, real mutation/edit proxies and JSON handoff. Each repeats three filesystem retention rounds with 200 future-mtime siblings and immediate successful citation; serving/reporting leaves item/history bytes unchanged. The first scratch matrix used an unsupported JSON plus section combination and failed at that usage validation; corrected valid markdown requests passed all four combinations without deadline changes. The unchanged release check and changelog check are now linked alongside both original receipt commands, all with 240-second deadlines. Strict health passes with pre-existing stale-owner and provenance advisories; validation retains metadata, resolution, missing-path and other-item trust warnings, with no item/history drift. Final archive consumers, linked checks and frozen-byte verification must pass before pushing only the existing PR branch. Releasing only this agent's claim for metadata freeze; owner remains in_progress for orchestrator decisions."
  "2026-10-10T12:15:00.898Z",codex-sol,"Final direct release check passes, but the newly linked full release command failed under the real schema-context environment: legacy test fixtures in context-pack and coverage-gaps passed only cwd to SDK init, so the linked tracker path took precedence and initialization refused or selected unrelated synthetic items. The original two receipt commands and changelog check still pass. Preserve the failed linked receipt, pin explicit cwd and pmRoot in those real initialization fixtures, and repeat all unchanged gates and deadlines. No history reconciliation or source coverage exception is involved. The earlier freeze is superseded; no push has occurred."
  "2026-10-10T12:17:18.058Z",codex-sol,"The first final linked release run executed 295 tests with 256 passes and 39 failures under schema context. Pinning initialization reduced this to 273 passes and 22 failures; those remaining item-creation calls still selected the injected tracker. All 39 initialization and 24 item-creation boundaries now supply explicit cwd and pmRoot. Repeating pm test with all four linked commands passes: nine receipt tests, one built acceptance test, full unchanged release check (295 passes, zero failures/skips) and changelog check. No runtime logic, assertion, test count, threshold or deadline changed. Repeated broad c8 observation retains 3809/3857 statements/lines, 1154/1160 branches and 103/104 functions. Failed receipts remain available separately. Commit this real fixture isolation repair with the owner evidence before the renewed final metadata freeze."
notes[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-25T23:12:05.165Z",pi-agent,"Design: register governed context_relevance service override that nudges pm's default ranking with a recency-decayed usage affinity derived from an append-only JSONL ledger at runtime/context-usage.jsonl. Auto-touch loop reads previous serve row + history/*.jsonl (ts field) to record touches for served items mutated since the last serve. New pm context-usage command for inspection/manual touch/reset. Fail-open returns undefined on any error."
  "2026-07-25T23:12:11.002Z",pi-agent,"Acceptance criteria: (1) context_relevance service registered via api.registerService returning {id,score}[] for every candidate. (2) Ledger at runtime/context-usage.jsonl bounded to 2000 rows, corrupt lines skipped. (3) Affinity in [0,1], neutral for unseen items, served-but-untouched below unserved. (4) Auto-touch from previous serve row + history ts. (5) pm context-usage command with --report/--touch/--reset/--json/--limit/--pm-path. (6) Fail-open returns undefined, never throws. (7) 100% coverage of new code. (8) manifest.json services capability added. (9) Four functional proofs in /tmp workspace."
  "2026-07-25T23:40:29.163Z",claude,"SCOPE CHANGE. The original design (a governed context_relevance service override plus a hand-rolled usage ledger) was discarded before implementation because it duplicated and would have corrupted shipped pm behaviour. pm 2026.7.25 already maintains runtime/context-usage.jsonl itself and already folds it into the usage_affinity signal of its built-in relevance model. The discarded draft wrote to that exact filename with an incompatible row schema ({t,at,id} vs pms {kind,at,author,item_id,intent}), so two writers with two schemas would have silently corrupted the signal both depend on."
  "2026-07-25T23:40:29.468Z",claude,"DELIVERED: read-only pm context-usage. Reports serve-then-touch conversion, waste (served but never touched = context paid for and unused) and misses (touched but never served = ranking failed to surface it), plus a per-item rollup. Deliberately does NOT compute a competing affinity score: pm owns the decay model, and a second implementation could silently disagree with the ranking it claims to explain. Flags: --author --surface --since --limit --format; the global --json is honoured."
  "2026-07-25T23:40:29.780Z",claude,"Acceptance: (1) 100/100/100/100 coverage on context-usage.ts via c8. (2) Registration and command execution tested through the SDKs own host harness (activateExtensionForTest / createExtensionTestHarness) instead of hand-built api doubles, so manifest capability governance is enforced in tests. (3) Verified against the real CLI on a live tracker: 33.3% conversion, 3 waste items, filters and rc=2 usage errors all correct. (4) index.ts api/ctx now typed with SDK ExtensionApi and CommandHandlerContext instead of any."
  "2026-07-25T23:40:30.130Z",claude,"Upstream issues filed from this work: pm-cli#717 (extensions cannot import the runtime SDK; ExtensionCommandSdk is the right mechanism but omits the derived-state readers) and pm-cli#719 (extension flags colliding with a pm global flag are silently shadowed - found by real-CLI testing after unit tests passed against a permissive double)."
  "2026-07-25T23:54:38.056Z",claude,"CodeRabbit review round 1 found two real defects, both fixed. P1: serves counted every ranked row, so an item pm ranked but cut from the pack was reported as waste - contradicting the modules own stated semantics, and my test had codified the wrong result. Now serves counts only included rows and a separate ranked column exposes budget losses (ranked - serves). P2: parseLedgerLine validated at as a string only, while every window filter, bound and conversion check compares timestamps lexically; \"...00.500Z\" sorts BEFORE \"...00Z\" because . precedes Z, so a non-canonical spelling silently inverted chronological order. Now requires canonical toISOString form."
